From 6187876fcab9ddb0b548b9c601d792260f6b9f2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:22:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 015/638] gfx: reject unsupported AROS native pixmap transfer
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: NativePixmapHandle only owns transferable backing objects on Linux/ChromeOS and Fuchsia. AROS has plane metadata but no native pixmap ownership or IPC transport, so the generic clone routine stopped the build at an unsupported-OS branch.

FIX_REASON: Keep empty handles valid for the software headless graph, but reject any non-empty AROS native pixmap clone instead of copying metadata and pretending the backing storage was transferred. Emit the rejected plane geometry through Chromium logging for AROS debug.resource visibility.

SCOPE: ui/gfx NativePixmapHandle IPC cloning.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j4 obj/ui/gfx/memory_buffer_sources/native_pixmap_handle.o

RISK: low for software headless rendering; native GPU pixmap sharing remains deliberately unavailable until AROS defines an ownership-bearing handle and Mojo transport.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.cc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.cc b/ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.cc
index a27f45bd7f..7fea791e5c 100644
--- a/ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.cc
+++ b/ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.cc
@@ -108,6 +108,11 @@ NativePixmapHandle CloneHandleForIPC(const NativePixmapHandle& handle) {
     cloned_plane.size = plane.size;
     cloned_plane.vmo = std::move(vmo_dup);
     clone.planes.push_back(std::move(cloned_plane));
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+    LOG(ERROR) << "AROS native pixmap IPC transport is not implemented"
+               << " (stride=" << plane.stride << ", offset=" << plane.offset
+               << ", size=" << plane.size << ")";
+    return NativePixmapHandle();
 #else
 #error Unsupported OS
 #endif
